### Health check
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/health

### Valid submission
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_id": "emp_123",
  "amount": 45.50,
  "category": "meals",
  "description": "Client lunch meeting",
  "expense_date": "2026-09-01"
}

### Invalid submission (bad category, should fail with 422)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_id": "emp_123",
  "amount": 45.50,
  "category": "snacks",
  "description": "Client lunch meeting",
  "expense_date": "2026-09-01"
}

### Test 1: Small amount — should auto-approve
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_id": "emp_1",
  "amount": 20,
  "category": "meals",
  "description": "Team lunch outing",
  "expense_date": "2026-09-01"
}

### Test 2: Mid-range with receipt — should need AI review
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_id": "emp_1",
  "amount": 300,
  "category": "travel",
  "description": "Client site visit travel",
  "expense_date": "2026-09-01",
  "receipt_url": "http://example.com/receipt1.pdf"
}

### Test 3: Huge amount — should auto-reject
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_id": "emp_1",
  "amount": 6000,
  "category": "travel",
  "description": "Company retreat booking",
  "expense_date": "2026-09-01",
  "receipt_url": "http://example.com/receipt2.pdf"
}

### LLM Test 1: Clear approve (high confidence expected)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_id": "emp_1",
  "amount": 180,
  "category": "travel",
  "description": "Uber rides to client office for 3-day onsite visit",
  "expense_date": "2026-09-01",
  "receipt_url": "http://example.com/receipt.pdf"
}

### LLM Test 2: Vague description (low confidence expected → human review)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_id": "emp_2",
  "amount": 520,
  "category": "client_entertainment",
  "description": "Team gathering expenses",
  "expense_date": "2026-09-01",
  "receipt_url": "http://example.com/receipt.pdf"
}

### LLM Test 3: Suspicious personal expense (high confidence reject expected)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_id": "emp_3",
  "amount": 300,
  "category": "other",
  "description": "Personal shopping items for home",
  "expense_date": "2026-09-01",
  "receipt_url": "http://example.com/receipt.pdf"
}

POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_id": "emp_5",
  "amount": 150,
  "category": "meals",
  "description": "Dinner but not sure if client was present",
  "expense_date": "2026-09-01",
  "receipt_url": "http://example.com/receipt.pdf"
}

### Get all pending human review expenses
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/review/pending

### Approve an expense (replace EXPENSE_ID with real id from above)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/review/a4e7b83c-a3de-4dc2-82c2-c8631555cf3e/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "manager_id": "manager_john",
  "note": "Verified with employee, legitimate business expense"
}

### Reject an expense (replace EXPENSE_ID with real id from above)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/review/EXPENSE_ID/reject
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "manager_id": "manager_john",
  "note": "Description too vague, cannot verify business purpose"
}